Package: napi-avahi
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: avahi-daemon, avahi-utils
Maintainer: NapiLab <info@napilab.ru>
Homepage: https://github.com/lab240/napi-avahi
Description: Find NAPI boards on the LAN without knowing their IP
 Gives the board the mDNS name napi<SoC>-<id>.local (napi3308-79df.local,
 napi3568-1c2e.local) and announces the service _napi._tcp with TXT records:
 model, SoC, OS, role, MAC, chip serial, kernel. The id is 4 hex of the md5
 of the chip serial: the MACs repeat between boards. The name and the records are refreshed at
 every boot; the system hostname is not changed.
 .
 Settings: /etc/napi/avahi.conf, or "napi-avahi role donoff,mgate" and
 "napi-avahi name <name>". All boards: "napi-avahi list" here, napi-finder.exe
 on Windows.
